Changelog: 20-11-2026 15:09:02

Added. A card Prime95 (mprime) among the machine's updates, when mprime is in ~/mprime: the release named in
~/mprime/.release against the one mersenne.org's download page lists. Its Update, and Fix, run Board Test's
installer (install-requirements.sh --mprime), which installs that release over the old one. An mprime unpacked by
hand has no release name: the card says so and Update installs the latest. The hourly reminder names it with the
other updates.

Changelog: 20-11-2026 14:57:33

Fixed. The catalog says PS5 SFTP Tools wants paramiko >=5.0,<6, as the app's requirements.txt now does.

Changelog: 20-11-2026 14:49:35

Fixed. Fix no longer asks pip for a version that cannot exist. A known vulnerability whose fix is a release above
what the app accepts (paramiko 5.0.0 for an app that wants >=3.4,<5) made the requirement
"paramiko>=3.4,<5,>=5.0.0", and pip found no version for it. Such an update is left out of Fix, and the package's
advice says which release fixes it, what the app accepts, and that a newer version of the app has to come first.
The card keeps its vulnerabilities.

Changelog: 20-11-2026 14:23:36

Fixed. mprime is found where its download is unpacked: ~/mprime/mprime, ~/.local/bin/mprime, /opt/mprime/mprime and
/usr/local/bin/mprime, the places PS5 CPU Tools looks in. It was looked for on PATH alone, so an mprime the app
used showed as Not installed. Its card's link to the manual now leads to the commands that install it
(docs/apps/cores.md, Installing mprime).

Changelog: 20-11-2026 02:18:33

Fixed. The catalog pins Vita3K build 4377 and Xenia Canary build 54386cb (19-11-2026), the builds the managers now
install.

Changelog: 20-11-2026 01:14:33

Added. The catalog knows PS5 CU Tools and PS5 CPU Tools: their launchers, and the tools they use (umr, memtest_vulkan, stress-ng, vkpeak, vkmark, glmark2, setpci, lspci, taskset, mprime, ras-mc-ctl, sudo, journalctl, and systemctl and PyQt6 as the other apps), as they came from its twin.

Changelog: 19-11-2026 21:46:13

Added. Nexus Deps knows a flattened Bazzite (no /run/ostree-booted, such as a PS5 image, where rpm-ostree refuses with "not booted via libostree"). Its Bazzite card shows the version from /etc/os-release and the running kernel, and nothing waits for a reboot. A System packages (dnf) card takes the place of Bazzite image: dnf check-update lists what is newer, the kernel too, and Update runs pkexec dnf upgrade -y. Fix installs a missing Fedora package with pkexec dnf install -y, there at once. A dnf step's question lists each package with a checkbox, all checked, and only the checked ones are installed or updated; a new kernel is used after a restart, which the question says. The texts say board, not console. The wiki's Nexus Deps chapter describes it.

Changelog: 15-11-2026 10:50:24

Added. The Sony cards: DualSense firmware (with PS5 Controller), PS4 system software
(Sony's update list), PS5 system software and PlayStation Portal (on the device), each with how to update.

Changelog: 15-11-2026 10:17:45

Breaking. One suite (owner, 15-11-2026): the repository is the suite, so --suite is gone, the catalog is
catalogs/bazzite-console.toml, and catalogs/upstreams.json lists an app without its suite. An upstream's card names
the app alone.

Breaking. No VERSION (owner, 15-11-2026): a development app is never released, so its header names the checkout's
last commit and its time ("5fb1aa8 · 15-11-2026 07:20", core's nexus.header()) where it showed a version, and
--version prints the same. The GitHub requests say nexus-deps.

Fixed. The app imports bazzite_console_core directly, with the Nexus design from core's nexus.py (owner,
15-11-2026): the compatibility package dev/core_compat is gone, and run.sh puts only core/ on the path.

Fixed. The code for Decky Loader is gone: the suite has no Decky app, and its loader.py glob matched the webcam's
firmware loader. The catalog lists core and its PyQt6, as core/pyproject.toml asks. Rust's card names Remote Play's
native core.

Changelog: 15-11-2026 06:25:22

Fixed. The catalog names Board Test by its new key, board, as apps.toml does: it said bazzite, so every check
stopped on "PyQt6 names board, which has no [app.board]".

Changelog: 15-11-2026 04:16:24

Fixed. Names the suite's renamed apps by their names, ids and keys where it mentions them (owner, 15-11-2026): PS5
Board Test, PS5 Bluetooth, PS5 CEC Manager, PS5 Fan Controller, PS5 DatStation, PS5 SFTP Tools, PS5 Webcam, PS5 SSD
Check, PS5 System Overlay, PS5 Controller and PS5 Upscaler Manager.

Changelog: 14-11-2026 12:11:51

Fixed. The window's text says the console where it said the board, and an app that changes the system is
called that.

Changelog: 14-11-2026 03:27:00

Breaking. Windows support is removed: the suite is for Bazzite. run.sh takes the Linux venv alone (it no longer
looks for a Windows venv under Git Bash). Nothing changes on Linux.

Changelog: 14-11-2026 00:36:00

Fixed. The emulator cards no longer fail with "HTTP Error 403: rate limit exceeded". GitHub was asked without a
sign-in, which allows 60 requests an hour for the whole address; the requests now carry the token of the machine's
gh login (or GITHUB_TOKEN, GH_TOKEN), 5,000 an hour, and a token GitHub refuses is left out. When the limit is used
up the card says until when, and how to sign in. The tests no longer ask GitHub or gh.

Changelog: 13-11-2026 22:48:09

Fixed. Packages installed in a venv's lib64/ are found. On Fedora with Python 3.15 a venv's lib64/ is a folder of
its own, not a link to lib/, and pip puts packages with compiled parts there: PyQt6 and PyQt6-Charts were reported
missing in every app's venv while they were installed.

Changelog: 13-11-2026 21:54:16

Fixed. The catalog of the Bazzite Console Suite knows the suite's three new apps and what they need: System Overlay,
Fan Control and HDMI CEC Manager with their PyQt6, pkexec, systemctl and notify-send for Fan Control's thermal guard,
systemctl and cec-ctl (v4l-utils, which Fix can layer) for HDMI CEC Manager, and PyQt6-Charts for Bazzite Test, which
its requirements.txt names. An installed app the catalog did not list was not checked at all. New in the catalog too:
the FFmpeg inside Remote Play's native core. The check for it asked a module that is not this suite's
(bazzite_console_link_core); it asks ps5_remoteplay_core, the core Remote Play imports, in the app's own venv. The
tests are this suite's again: 31 of them still asked for the tools, apps and names of the suite the app came from
(stress-ng, setpci, flashrom, Decky Loader, Sony's firmware lists, "nexus-suite") and failed. They read this suite's
catalog now, and the checks it has no tool for (a tool that needs root, one of two commands, flashrom's internal
programmer, Homebrew before rpm-ostree, Decky and Sony's lists) run on entries the tests make themselves.

